WEBVTT

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.310
Well, here we are, the Australian Grand Prix.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:11.060
This is the track, Adelaide, a scorcher, 30 degrees, and this is it, and I would like

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.920
to say welcome to Adelaide.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:27.290
For the Formula One teams, used to the easy access of racing in Europe, Australia is literally

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.410
the other end of the earth.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.000
By virtue of...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.420
an aggressive approach to Foka, South Australia has brought World Championship Grand Prix

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.800
Racing to the land down under.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:01:00.000
As the festival state, and with a reputation for producing world-class wines from the Barossa

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:06.380
it has involved a major change of image to entertain the glamorous Grand Prix circus.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.650
Having travelled so far to race, the teams will appreciate the state's capital city,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.340
Adelaide.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.950
International standard accommodation in the centre of the city is only two kilometres

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:22.380
from the circuit, a trip of under a minute for a top-class driver in a qualifying mood.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.620
In this age of tar and cement cities, Adelaide is a rare mixture of charming old buildings

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.000
and park lands.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.180
circuit winds through the picturesque East Park lands and the Victoria Park

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.390
Racecourse is skillfully incorporated to house the pit area and a short

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.540
straight. There will be plenty of vantage points for spectators around the

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.610
3.8 kilometre track and there'll be no shortage of fans flocking to the city of

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:52.250
churches for this historic race. Adelaide is a city with a conservative population

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.620
used to Sunday's peace being disturbed only by the ringing of church bells.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.510
But this isn't just any Sabbath.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.940
This is Sunday, Bloody Beauty, Grand Prix Sunday.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.010
Ian Chappell welcoming viewers around the world

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.070
to the city of Adelaide,

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.190
a city that's certainly come alive this afternoon.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.410
And there he is, the young Brazilian favourite for the race,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.730
the man who's grabbed pole position there in centre.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.500
He's grabbed it six times already this season.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.000
This is his...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.380
seventh he's going to be 10 times in the front row of the grid that's pretty impressive Ayrton

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:40.260
Senna the man to beat with regards to everybody else right now but on the second fastest starting

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.840
position a man who's won the last two Grand Prix and that's the Englishman Nigel Mann so he's got

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:57.000
to be hot. Keke Rosberg former world champion Keke Rosberg the man who will be third off the

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
grid here this afternoon and the man to bring you all the action.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.980
here in the Australian Grand Prix, Murray Walker and James Hunt.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:21.520
Yes, Adelaide is alive in 30 degree heat on the finest street circuit in the world.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:27.650
All is set for Australia's first ever World Championship Grand Prix in front of a sellout

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.000
capacity crowd of well over one.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.380
100,000 people, and there's one of the men

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.020
that they will be watching most of all today.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.520
In third position on the grid, that was Keki Rosberg.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.140
You are looking now at the unclothed car

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.290
of world champion Alain Prost.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.350
Fourth on the grid, but significantly,

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:54.450
second fastest in this morning's unofficial practice.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.410
There's Willy Dungal on the right,

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:00.000
